  "name": "24 HR URINARY FREE CORTISOL",
  "code": "1744",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Comment</span></strong><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Urine free cortisol (UFC) is a sensitive test for the various types of adrenocortical dysfunction, particularly </span><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">hypercortisolism. It is the preferred screening test for Cushing syndrome. Most patients with Cushing </span><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">syndrome have increased 24-hour urinary excretion of cortisol.</span><br><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Clinical Use</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Evaluate Adrenal function</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Marker for apparent mineralocorticoid excess syndrome</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Additional marker for exogenous steroid use</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Increased Levels - Cushing &lsquo;s syndrome, stress, late pregnancy, ACTH secreting tumor</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Decreased Levels - Addison&rsquo;s disease, Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia, Hypopituitarism</span></p>",
